Milestone: Reusable cooperative runtime and independent eye tuning
Dependencies: 01_RESEARCH_AND_DESIGN.todo
Purpose: Reuse the actual CLI pipeline without blocking Qt or maintaining a second compositor.

Tasks:
  [x] Share validated per-eye blink/wink rules between actions and both renderers.
  [x] Preserve global CLI thresholds and add independent left/right overrides.
  [x] Add cooperative stop, bounded logs/preview, telemetry, and live tuning hooks.
  [x] Preserve clean export, freeze behavior, headless semantics, and resource cleanup.
  [x] Exercise fake capture/tracker lifecycle and per-eye regression cases.

Acceptance criteria:
  A threshold edit changes rendered K/C eyes and detection without restarting the camera.
  Invalid settings are explicit; edits are applied as one validated immutable snapshot.
  Renderer/GL allocation and release stay on the worker thread.
  Partial initialization failure closes already acquired resources.
  Existing CLI tests remain valid.

Completion evidence:
  tests\test_studio_runtime.py; per-eye cases in tracking/renderer/CLI tests.
  Full suite: 220 passed; Ruff passed on 2026-11-02.
  Real offline GUI/MediaPipe/GPU replay completed without opening a live camera.
